  "articleBody": "It's tempting to rush through a remodeling project, but skipping steps, especially when it comes to countertop installation, can lead to real headaches down the road. One of the biggest mistakes we see is templating for countertops too early, before the space is truly ready. If your cabinets aren't properly installed, level, and secured, you're setting yourself up for disaster. Imagine a beautiful new multi-height countertop that's wobbly or uneven – not ideal, right? Changing your layout or appliance choices after templating is another common pitfall. This can cause delays, extra costs, and a lot of frustration because the fabricated countertop won't fit correctly. Also, ignoring issues with support for overhangs or not planning your seam placement can create structural problems and affect the aesthetic of your new counters. You definitely don’t want a gorgeous stone slab cracking because it wasn’t supported properly! These kinds of errors can force expensive rework and seriously delay your whole project. That’s why it’s so important to have a professional handle these complex installations, especially when you have multiple elevations or heavy materials. HH Remodeling LLC has the experience to ensure your multi-height countertops are installed correctly the first time.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
